==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|persecutio|persecūtio|chase, pursuit|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|persequor||follow up, pursue|lang=la}}, from {{prefix|per|sequor|t1=through|t2=follow|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-persecution.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# The act of [[persecute|persecuting]].
# A [[program]] or [[campaign]] to [[subjugate]] or [[eliminate]] a [[specific]] group of [[people]], often based on [[race]], [[religion]], [[sexuality]], or [[social]] [[beliefs]].
#*{{quote-magazine|year=2012|month=March-April
|author={{w|Jan Sapp}}
|title=Race Finished
|volume=100|issue=2|page=164
|magazine={{w|American Scientist}}
|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/race-finished
|passage=Few concepts are as emotionally charged as that of race. The word conjures up a mixture of associations—culture, ethnicity, genetics, subjugation, exclusion and '''persecution'''. But is the tragic history of efforts to define groups of people by race really a matter of the misuse of science, the abuse of a valid biological concept?}}

